hey there fellow townscapers and welcome  back to the channel if this is your  first time here welcome welcome welcome  and thank you so much for stopping by it  is always appreciated when you guys stop  by to see what i'm doing  so today's video is about a new  up-and-coming city builder game but  before we talk about it i want to talk  about the paint over contest i want to  congratulate the first two paint over  contest winners my drill keys and blue  mizel they did amazing work and you can  see their entries in the gallery on the  website we also have a new entry from  the dank boy and i really really like  their work as you can see it's a  watercolor paint over and i think it was  executed very well i love watercolor so  i think it was a very beautiful job you  can view their entry on the gallery also  if you want to win a free copy of  townscaper for you or a friend you can  enter by clicking the link in the  description the video will tell you  everything that you need to know about  entering so you'll know how to access  the entry form and how to submit your  photos  so now that we've gotten that out the  way let's get into what we're all here  for i broke my own rule  if you look on my about page you will  see that this channel is solely  dedicated to townscaper almost like a  shrine if you will but today i want to  talk about castrudo i was contacted by  daniel wolfson the creator of costrudo  and i was asked to test the program and  i gladly accepted i'm obsessed with city  building games so it was a no-brainer  for me so let's just get right into it  and let's talk about it costrudo is  about building your dream italian villa  placing block to block in the middle of  nowhere in the ocean you can choose your  style from more than five different  variations and there is no particular  essence of the game you just need to  keep calm and build to the relaxing  wildfire music i like castrudo because  it's very chill i like the texture of  the structures and as you can see it  really looks like an italian villa it  has the shutters on your windows and the  drainage pipes on the side to really  give you that realistic feel the music  is beautiful as a fan of lo-fi i really  enjoy the soundtrack there are eight  lo-fi tracks so you have a nice set of  music to build to there's also an active  daylight cycle and you can change the  time of day also by using this dial here  so you can literally build from dusk  until dawn which i just love i think  that's my favorite part and i also think  that is a very nice touch of realism as  well the water also looks great and i  love watching it move as the sun rises  and sets on my builds cosrudo is  currently in beta so there are limits to  the game such as build height and grid  size but there are features that will be  added later  after testing i spoke with daniel and i  asked him some questions about the  development of castruto and you know  just what to expect in the near future  so daniel has informed me that there are  plans to add more settings modding  capabilities more specifically the steam  workshop could be involved and there are  also plans for a campaign random map  generation and much more some things  that i would personally like to see  would be keyboard controls and the  ability to add custom music almost like  how you use self radio on grand theft  auto you know how you would take your  music files and you put them into a  folder and the game will pull those  files from the folder and they will play  them for you i honestly think that would  be nice i also think it would be nice to  have a longer daylight cycle the  daylight cycle is about two minutes long  which isn't bad however more daylight is  good i think maybe it could be a setting  where you could adjust the time to your  preference and i think that would be  very cool so if you want it to be longer  if you want your day to be 10 minutes  long you could do so if you wanted to be  less than two minutes you could do that  as well i'm gonna show you guys some  gameplay you know just so you can get an  idea of what castrudo is like if you  enjoy this video and you want to try out  costrudo it will be available to the  public on the 16th of february and  that's this coming wednesday so you can  mark your calendar or you can make it  easier on yourself and you can add it to  your wish list the link is in the  description below so you can just go in  the description you can click on that  link and the link will take you to steam  and if you're logged in you can just add  it to that wishlist well that is all i  have for today but i will leave you all  with the gameplay so you can see  castrito for yourself i hope you all  enjoy it remember that all the important  links are in the description below i  want to thank you guys so much for  stopping by i can't stress that enough i  really really appreciate all the love  and support if you enjoyed this content  please like the video and share it with  people that you know would enjoy it as  well also please subscribe as it does  help me out a lot i'm almost at 2 000  subscribers and i can't do it without  you guys and i would really really  really really appreciate it so please if  you can subscribe to the channel i would  be so grateful so with that being said  i'll let you all go and i will see you  guys next time  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  do  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  do  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

